# `/zh` is a language tree, not a host root: site-wide endpoints and generated
# assets have one canonical home at the root (robots/sitemaps are
# language-independent; the OG site card is brand-level and the card font has
# no CJK glyphs; the coordinate manifest is fetched by URL). Requests under
# `/zh` redirect instead of 404ing. The zh per-section agent indexes are real
# files (`src/pages/zh/[section]/llms.txt.ts`); the full-text corpus stays
# English, so `/zh/llms-full.txt` falls back to the zh agent index.
/zh/llms-full.txt /zh/llms.txt 301
/zh/og.png /og.png 301
/zh/og/* /og/:splat 301
/zh/robots.txt /robots.txt 301
/zh/sitemap-0.xml /sitemap-0.xml 301
/zh/sitemap-index.xml /sitemap-index.xml 301
/zh/nimbus-api/* /nimbus-api/:splat 301
